# Documentation Linking Strategy

- When adding internal markdown links, it's okay to link to documentation pages that haven't been created yet (e.g., `[Attribute](../Attribute.md)`).
- These links act as placeholders and will generate Docusaurus warnings initially.
- As the target documentation files (like `Attribute.md`) are created in the correct location, these links should resolve automatically.
- Keep an eye on Docusaurus build warnings to track which documentation pages still need to be created to resolve all links.

