# Documentation Version Context

- All documentation should explicitly reference the version of the data-exploration codebase it pertains to.
- Include version-specific details, such as:
  - The specific commit hash or tag of the data-exploration repository.
  - Any version-specific features, behaviors, or limitations.
  - Changes or updates that might affect the documented functionality.
- This ensures that users can match the documentation to the correct version of the codebase they are using.
